cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "HTN: Hierarchical Tensor Networks for Lattice Models"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself
  and the accompanying paper (see preferred-citation).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Akimenko
    given-names: "S. S."
    email: iakobian@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Omsk State Technical University, Omsk, Russian Federation"
  - family-names: Myshlyavtsev
    given-names: "A. V."
    affiliation: "Omsk State Technical University, Omsk, Russian Federation"
repository-code: "https://github.com/IakOBiaN/HTN"
abstract: >-
  Python implementation of the Hierarchical Tensor Network (HTN)
  approach for computing thermodynamic properties of statistical-physics
  models (Ising, binary lattice gas) on hierarchical lattices such as the
  diamond-like hierarchical lattice (DHL) and the folded square
  hierarchical lattice (FSHL).
keywords:
  - tensor networks
  - hierarchical lattices
  - statistical physics
  - renormalization group
  - Ising model
  - lattice gas
  - adsorption
license: MIT
